{
  "name": "Z — cost plan in time, tender-price inflation allowance, curve-aware package timing, VAT-charged package",
  "kind": "programme",
  "note": "R15b spec §24. The corpus's first document to carry a QS-provenanced tender-price inflation allowance (`cost_plan.qs.inflation`), a non-straight-line phase feeding the cost plan (`mande_fitout`, `back_loaded`), a per-package `price_basis` classification exercised end to end, a package-level VAT override that actually charges (`pkg-externals`, with `vat.registered: true` switched on to make it live), and a percentage-of-construction-total fee line whose base is the INFLATED construction total.\n\nZ is fixture S (`s-dated-programme.json`, migrated to `inputs_version: 14`) with the changes in test-cases.md §24.1's table and no other: the QS record; the new `mande_fitout` phase (SS construction + 3, back-loaded, appended to `phases[]`); `pkg-mande.phase_id` retagged to it; `price_basis` set on all five packages; a VAT override on `pkg-externals`; `vat.registered` flipped true; and one new fee line, `fee-pm` (1% of construction total). Every other field is S's, unmoved.\n\nTHE COST-STACK PINS BELOW ARE HAND-DERIVED, independently of both engines, in test-cases.md §24.1 Steps 1-6 -- the package windows and curve-aware midpoints (Step 2), the inflation factor and pence per package (Step 3), the stack (base build, contingency, construction_total, the pct fee, professional_total, lender_eligible_ratio -- Step 4), the bucketed uses and the per-month lender-eligible SHARE computed from unrounded per-package spend rather than `spreadByCurve`'s rounded output (Step 5), and the VAT on the one overridden package (Step 6). THE LEDGER PINS (funding_gap_pence, peak_debt_pence, peak_debt_month, finance_costs_pence, total_development_cost_pence, the profit and LTC/LTGDV figures, senior_breakeven_pence, the redemption schedule and the cost-to-complete summary) are the two engines' AGREED figures -- run only after the cost-stack pins above were fixed from the worksheet, with the named months in §24.1 Step 5's share table hand-checked rather than merely trusted from the run.\n\nZ's companion, §24.2, re-pins fixture S itself under the same calc 2.16.0 engine: S's per-month lender-eligible SHARE is a clean 0.9 in its main window (no rounding boundary -- deliberately, as S's own note states of its cost stack), so its funding gap has a closed form: 6 x 1,055,000 = 6,330,000, up from the R14 uniform-ratio figure of 6,300,000 because full funding now concentrates onto the strip-out months instead of being shaved everywhere. Z is registered in every fixture roster (`EXPECTED_FIXTURE_STEMS` on both sides, this document, and the v13 -> v14 identity gate's stored-version exclusion, which names it explicitly). It is the corpus's first v14-native document: it has no v13 antecedent, so it carries no v13 -> v14 comparison of its own, the same position Y held one release earlier for the v12 -> v13 gate.",
